When `forceFocus` is false (e.g. mouse click), this still calls `focusOnUIElement` with `poll: true`. Because the sidebar container isn’t normally focusable, this will poll for ~500ms and repeatedly attempt to focus but will never succeed, doing unnecessary work on every click. Consider skipping the focus call entirely when `forceFocus` is false, or set `poll: false` (and possibly `forceFocus: false`) for the non-keyboard path.
```suggestion
    if (forceFocus) {
      api.focusOnUIElement(focusableUIElements.sidebarRegion, {
        forceFocus: true,
        poll: true,
      });
    }
```
